@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+## TraderX State 017 Runtime
+
+This directory defines the compose runtime for:
+
+- `017-cdm-lifecycle-mapping`
+
+It starts from the state `009-order-management-matcher` runtime (compose project
+`traderx-state-017`), which extends pricing + observability runtime with:
+
+- Order matcher service (Spring Boot + DB-backed order persistence)
+- Order management APIs (`/order-matcher/orders*`)
+- Spring Boot actuator metric scraping (`/actuator/prometheus`) where available
+- Provisioned order + Spring dashboards for queue health, lifecycle rates, latency, and JVM/service SLI visibility
+
+State 017 adds:
+
+- `cdm-service` (port `18120`, ingress `/cdm-service/`): CDM master for parties, persons and
+  securities, plus the CDM order/trade lifecycle built from NATS order and trade events.
+  Its `/health` answers 200 only once the security and party masters are seeded, and the compose
+  healthcheck uses it. `account-service`, `people-service` and `reference-data` wait for it
+  (`CDM_SERVICE_URL=http://cdm-service:18120`).
+- Prometheus scrapes `cdm-service:18120/actuator/prometheus` in the `traderx-spring-boot-actuator` job.
+- The order matcher seeds only its `NEW` demo orders (`ORDER_MATCHER_SEED_STATUSES=NEW`; blank
+  = every status, the 009 seed). Seeded partially filled or filled orders have no booked trades,
+  so their CDM lineage could not be consistent.
+- At cdm-service startup (`CDM_LIFECYCLE_BACKFILL_ENABLED=true`) the seed trades in the `trades`
+  table are imported into CDM as direct trades, and the matcher's open orders
+  (`GET /orders?status=open`) that have no CDM proposal get proposed and accepted workflow steps.
+- cdm-service runs in UTC (`TZ=UTC`, `-Duser.timezone=UTC`) because it reads the zone-less
+  `trades.created` timestamps as UTC.
+
+Data volume:
+
+- Postgres data lives in the named volume `traderx-state-017_postgres_state_017_data`. The schema
+  (`postgres-init/initialSchema.sql`) is applied only when that volume is first created.
+- The start script checks an existing volume for the 017 schema (`cdm_documents` and related
+  tables, `trades.orderid`). If they are missing, it stops and asks you to rerun with
+  `--reset-data`, which removes the volume (all 017 orders, trades and CDM documents) and starts fresh.
+
+Ports:
+
+- 017 uses the same host ports as 009, so only one of them can run at a time. The start script
+  refuses to start while compose project `traderx-state-009` is running. Containers and volumes
+  are project-scoped (`traderx-state-017` vs `traderx-state-009`) and do not collide.
+
+Primary endpoints:
+
+- TraderX UI: `http://localhost:8080`
+- Grafana dashboards (via ingress): `http://localhost:8080/grafana/`
+- Grafana (direct): `http://localhost:3001`
+- Prometheus: `http://localhost:9090`
+- Loki: `http://localhost:3100`
+- Tempo: `http://localhost:3200`
+- NATS monitor: `http://localhost:8222/varz`
+- Price publisher: `http://localhost:18100/health`
+- Order matcher: `http://localhost:18110/health`
+- CDM service: `http://localhost:8080/cdm-service/health` (direct: `http://localhost:18120/health`)
+
+Grafana access:
+
+- Dashboards are anonymous Viewer surfaces through ingress for demos.
+- Local admin access is available at the direct Grafana URL.
+- The generated start script prints the active admin credential on startup.
+- Defaults are state-scoped: `TRADERX_GRAFANA_ADMIN_USER` falls back to `traderx-admin`; `TRADERX_GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD` falls back to `traderx-state-017`.
+- Override those values before startup for any shared or long-lived environment.
